//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @page c_tafKeyStore Key Store Service
 *
 * @ref taf_ks_interface.h "API Reference"
 *
 * <HR>
 * Key Store is an access control-based service with access to trusted hardware bound crypto. It
 * ensures all cryptographic keys generated are bound to the device crytographically and all crypto
 * operations are running in a trusted execution environment.
 *
 * Key Store service provides APIs to application for key management, key access control and crypto
 * operations. It has a built-in reliable and secure backend storage to save cryptographic keys
 * created by client applications. It also supports client authentication which means only the key
 * owner has the permission to access or use the key for certain purpose.
 *
 * @section taf_ks_binding IPC interfaces binding
 *
 * All the functions of this API are provided by the @b tafKeyStoreSvc application service.
 *
 * Here's a sample of how to bind to Key Store service:
 * @verbatim
   bindings:
   {
       clientExe.clientComponent.taf_ks -> tafKeyStoreSvc.taf_ks
   }
   @endverbatim
 *
 * @section c_taf_ks_key_management Key management
 *
 * A new key can be created by using taf_ks_CreateKey() with desired key name and key usage passed
 * as input parameters, a key reference as output parameter is returned to client for subsequent
 * operations.
 *
 * New keys initially have no value and cannot be used for any crypto operations. Application shall
 * call taf_ks_ProvisionXXX() API to provision or import the key value and save the key into backend
 * storage. Following key provision/import APIs are supported:
 * - taf_ks_ProvisionRsaEncKeyValue() - Provision or import a RSA encryption key value.
 * - taf_ks_ProvisionRsaSigKeyValue() - Provision or import a RSA signing key value.
 * - taf_ks_ProvisionAesKeyValue() - Provision or import an AES key value.
 * - taf_ks_ProvisionEcdsaKeyValue() - Provision or import an ECDSA key value.
 * - taf_ks_ProvisionHmacKeyValue() - Provision or import a HMAC key value.
 *
 * Here is an example of how an AES GCM key is created and provisioned:
 * @verbatim
   const char keyId[] = "MyAesGcmKey";
   taf_ks_KeyRef_t keyRef;
   if (LE_NOT_FOUND == taf_ks_GetKey(keyId, &keyRef))
   {
       LE_ASSERT(LE_OK == taf_ks_CreateKey(keyId,TAF_KS_AES_ENCRYPT_DECRYPT, &keyRef));
       LE_ASSERT(LE_OK == taf_ks_ProvisionAesKeyValue(keyRef,
                                                      TAF_KS_AES_SIZE_256,
                                                      TAF_KS_AES_MODE_GCM,
                                                      NULL, 0));
   }
   @endverbatim
 *
 * @note A key only allows one-shot provisioning after creation.
 *
 * Optionally, application can call taf_ks_SetKeyXXX() to set the attribute of key access control
 * before key provisioning. Following key access control APIs are supported:
 * - taf_ks_SetKeyMaxUsesPerBoot() - Set the maximum number of times that a key can be used per
 *   system boot.
 * - taf_ks_SetKeyMinSecondsBetweenOps() - Set the minimum amount of time that elapses between
 *   allowed cryptographic operations using a key.
 * - taf_ks_SetKeyActiveDateTime() - Set the date and time at which the key becomes active. Prior to
 *   this time any attempt to use the key will fail.
 * - taf_ks_SetKeyOriginationExpireDateTime() - Set the date and time at which the key expires for
 *   signing and encryption. After this time any attempt to use a key for signing or encryption will
 *   fail.
 * - taf_ks_SetKeyUsageExpireDateTime() - Set the date and time at which the key expires for
 *   verification and decryption. After this time any attempt to use a key for verification and
 *   decryption will fail.
 *
 * @note currently all the key access control APIs are not implemented yet.
 *
 * Call taf_ks_GetKey() to get key reference by key name, call taf_ks_GetKeyUsage() to get the key
 * usage by key reference.
 *
 * @note taf_ks_GetKey() will return LE_NOT_FOUND if the key is created but not provisioned yet.
 *
 * Call taf_ks_DeleteKey() to delete a key from the backend storage.
 *
 * @section c_taf_ks_crypto_operation Cryptographic operation
 *
 * The typical use cases are data encryption/decryption and message signing/verification. Each
 * crypto operation must be processed within a context. A crypto session bound to the context must
 * be created to use a key for certain cryptographic operation.
 *
 * @subsection c_taf_ks_create_session Create and start context session
 * Call taf_ks_CryptoSessionCreate() to create a session and get session reference for subsequent
 * operations.
 *
 * Call taf_ks_CryptoSessionSetAesNonce() to set the NONCE specifically for the AES CBC/CTR/GCM key.
 *
 * Call taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart() to start the session.
 *
 * Here is an example of how to create a crypto session and start the session for data encryption:
 * @verbatim
   taf_ks_CryptoSessionRef_t sessionRef;
   const uint8_t nonce[12] = {"abcdefghijk"}; // Shall be customized and filled by application.
   LE_ASSERT(LE_OK == taf_ks_CryptoSessionCreate(keyRef, &sessionRef));
   LE_ASSERT(LE_OK == taf_ks_CryptoSessionSetAesNonce(sessionRef, nonce, sizeof(nonce)));
   LE_ASSERT(LE_OK == taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart(sessionRef, TAF_KS_CRYPTO_ENCRYPT));
   @endverbatim
 *
 * @subsection c_taf_ks_process_session Process data within the session
 * Call taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcess() to process the input data and get the output data in a running
 * crypto session started with taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart(). It shall be called for multiple times if
 * the input data size is greater than TAF_KS_MAX_PACKET_SIZE, which means the input data shall be
 * split into small pieces with the size of each piece less than TAF_KS_MAX_PACKET_SIZE.
 *
 * @note For AES GCM key, taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcessAead() must be called for one time or multiple
 * times to pass the AEAD before calling taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcess(). taf_ks_CryptoSessionAbort()
 * is used to abort a running session if needed.
 *
 * Call taf_ks_CryptoSessionEnd() to normally finish the cryptographic operation in the running
 * session after all input data get processed by taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcess().
 *
 * Here is an example of how to process the input plain text and get the encrypted data, the
 * encrypted data will be saved in the byte array of @b encryptedData with size of @b totalEncSize .
 * @verbatim
   const uint8_t plainText[] = "Keystore service for AES GCM test messages.";
   uint8_t encryptedData[TAF_KS_MAX_PACKET_SIZE] = {0};
   size_t encryptedDataSize = sizeof(encryptedData);
   const uint8_t aead[] = {"123456789"}; // Shall be customized and filled by application.
   LE_ASSERT(LE_OK == taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcessAead(sessionRef, aead, sizeof(aead)));
   LE_ASSERT(LE_OK == taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcess(sessionRef,
                                                  plainText,
                                                  sizeof(plainText),
                                                  encryptedData,
                                                  &encryptedDataSize));
   size_t totalEncSize = encryptedDataSize;
   encryptedDataSize = sizeof(encryptedData) - totalEncSize;
   LE_ASSERT(LE_OK == taf_ks_CryptoSessionEnd(sessionRef,
                                              NULL, 0,
                                              encryptedData + totalEncSize,
                                              &encryptedDataSize));
   totalEncSize = totalEncSize + encryptedDataSize;
   @endverbatim
 *
 * @note The crypto session is automatically deleted after the taf_ks_CryptoSessionAbort() or the
 * taf_ks_CryptoSessionEnd() is called, or when any error occurs in taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart() and
 * taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcess().
 *
 * <HR>
 *
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

USETYPES le_limit.api;

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * The maximum size of the key name in bytes.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFINE MAX_KEY_ID_SIZE = 256;

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * The maximum size of the secure label in bytes.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFINE MAX_SEC_LABEL_SIZE = 256;

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * The maximum size of the data packet in bytes.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFINE MAX_PACKET_SIZE = 4096;

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * The maximum nonce or IV size for AES GCM, CBC, CTR in bytes.
 *
 * AES GCM nonce size must be fixed length of 12 bytes. AES CBC/CTR IV size must be fixed length of
 * 16 bytes.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFINE MAX_AES_NONCE_SIZE = 16;

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * The minimum and maximum size for HMAC key in bytes.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFINE MIN_HMAC_KEY_SIZE = 8;
DEFINE MAX_HMAC_KEY_SIZE = 128;

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the supported RSA key size.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM RsaKeySize
{
    RSA_SIZE_1024 = 1, ///< RSA key size is 1024 bit
    RSA_SIZE_2048,     ///< RSA key size is 2048 bit
    RSA_SIZE_3072,     ///< RSA key size is 3072 bit
    RSA_SIZE_4096,     ///< RSA key size is 4096 bit
    RSA_SIZE_MAX,
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the supported AES key size.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM AesKeySize
{
    AES_SIZE_128 = 1,  ///< AES key size is 128 bit
    AES_SIZE_192,      ///< AES key size is 192 bit
    AES_SIZE_256,      ///< AES key size is 256 bit
    AES_SIZE_MAX,
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the supported ECC key size.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM EccKeySize
{
    ECC_SIZE_224 = 1,  ///< NIST/SECG curve over a 224 bit prime field
    ECC_SIZE_256,      ///< NIST/SECG curve over a 256 bit prime field
    ECC_SIZE_384,      ///< NIST/SECG curve over a 384 bit prime field
    ECC_SIZE_521,      ///< NIST/SECG curve over a 521 bit prime field
    ECC_SIZE_MAX,
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the key usage.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM KeyUsage
{
    RSA_ENCRYPT_DECRYPT,    ///< RSA key for encryption and decryption
    RSA_ENCRYPT_ONLY,       ///< RSA key for encryption only
    RSA_DECRYPT_ONLY,       ///< RSA key for decryption only
    RSA_SIGN_VERIFY,        ///< RSA key for signing and verification
    RSA_SIGN_ONLY,          ///< RSA key for signing only
    RSA_VERIFY_ONLY,        ///< RSA key for verification only
    AES_ENCRYPT_DECRYPT,    ///< AES key for encryption and decryption
    AES_ENCRYPT_ONLY,       ///< AES key for encryption only
    AES_DECRYPT_ONLY,       ///< AES key for decryption only
    ECDSA_SIGN_VERIFY,      ///< ECDSA key for signing and verification
    ECDSA_SIGN_ONLY,        ///< ECDSA key for signing only
    ECDSA_VERIFY_ONLY,      ///< ECDSA key for verfication only
    HMAC_SIGN_VERIFY,       ///< HMAC for signing and verification
    HMAC_SIGN_ONLY,         ///< HMAC for signing only
    HMAC_VERIFY_ONLY,       ///< HMAC for verification only
    KEYUSAGE_MAX,
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the crypto purpose for a cryptographic operation session.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM CryptoPurpose
{
    CRYPTO_ENCRYPT,         ///< Crypto operation for encryption
    CRYPTO_DECRYPT,         ///< Crypto operation for decryption
    CRYPTO_SIGN,            ///< Crypto operation for signing
    CRYPTO_VERIFY,          ///< Crypto operation for verify
    CRYPTO_MAX,
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the digest algorithms used by RSA, ECC and HMAC.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM Digest
{
    DIGEST_MD5 = 1,         ///< MD5
    DIGEST_SHA1,            ///< SHA1
    DIGEST_SHA2_224,        ///< SHA2-224
    DIGEST_SHA2_256,        ///< SHA2-256
    DIGEST_SHA2_384,        ///< SHA2-384
    DIGEST_SHA2_512,        ///< SHA2-512
    DIGEST_MAX,
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the padding type for RSA encryption key.
 *
 * The specified hash function used in MFG1 is only for OAEP padding
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM RsaEncPadding
{
    RSA_ENC_PAD_NONE,            ///< No padding
    RSA_ENC_PAD_PKCS1_V15,       ///< PKCS1 V1.5 padding
    RSA_ENC_PAD_OAEP_MD5,        ///< OAEP with MD5 padding
    RSA_ENC_PAD_OAEP_SHA1,       ///< OAEP with SHA1 padding
    RSA_ENC_PAD_OAEP_SHA2_224,   ///< OAEP with SHA2-224 padding
    RSA_ENC_PAD_OAEP_SHA2_256,   ///< OAEP with SHA2-256 padding
    RSA_ENC_PAD_OAEP_SHA2_384,   ///< OAEP with SHA2-384 padding
    RSA_ENC_PAD_OAEP_SHA2_512,   ///< OAEP with SHA2-512 padding
    RSA_ENC_PAD_MAX,
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the padding type for RSA signature key.
 *
 * The specified hash function used in MFG1 is for both PSS padding and digest to sign.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM RsaSigPadding
{
    RSA_SIG_PAD_NONE,               ///< No padding
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PKCS1_V15_MD5,      ///< PKCS1 V1.5 padding, digest is MD5
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PKCS1_V15_SHA1,     ///< PKCS1 V1.5 padding, digest is SHA1
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PKCS1_V15_SHA2_224, ///< PKCS1 V1.5 padding, digest is SHA2-224
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PKCS1_V15_SHA2_256, ///< PKCS1 V1.5 padding, digest is SHA2-256
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PKCS1_V15_SHA2_384, ///< PKCS1 V1.5 padding, digest is SHA2-384
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PKCS1_V15_SHA2_512, ///< PKCS1 V1.5 padding, digest is SHA2-512
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PSS_MD5,            ///< PSS with MD5 padding, digest is MD5
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PSS_SHA1,           ///< PSS with SHA1 padding, digest is SHA1
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PSS_SHA2_224,       ///< PSS with SHA2-224 padding, digest is SHA2-224
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PSS_SHA2_256,       ///< PSS with SHA2-256 padding, digest is SHA2-256
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PSS_SHA2_384,       ///< PSS with SHA2-384 padding, digest is SHA2-384
    RSA_SIG_PAD_PSS_SHA2_512,       ///< PSS with SHA2-512 padding, digest is SHA2-512
    RSA_SIG_PAD_MAX,
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Define the AES block mode.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM AesBlockMode
{
    AES_MODE_ECB_PAD_NONE,  ///< AES ECB mode without padding
    AES_MODE_ECB_PAD_PKCS7, ///< AES ECB mode with PKCS7 padding
    AES_MODE_CBC_PAD_NONE,  ///< AES CBC mode without padding
    AES_MODE_CBC_PAD_PKCS7, ///< AES CBC mode with PKCS7 padding
    AES_MODE_CTR,           ///< AES CTR mode
    AES_MODE_GCM,           ///< AES GCM mode
    AES_MODE_MAX
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Reference for key object.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REFERENCE Key;

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Reference for cryptographic operation session.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REFERENCE CryptoSession;

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Create a new key.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key already exists.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CreateKey
(
    string   keyName[MAX_KEY_ID_SIZE] IN, ///< Key name
    KeyUsage keyUsage                 IN, ///< Key usage
    Key      keyRef                   OUT ///< Key reference
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Get key by key name.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist or isn't provisioned yet.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetKey
(
    string keyName[MAX_KEY_ID_SIZE] IN, ///< Key name
    Key    keyRef                   OUT ///< Key reference
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Delete key by key reference.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key has running crypto session.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t DeleteKey
(
    Key    keyRef                   IN  ///< Key reference
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Get key usage.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetKeyUsage
(
    Key       keyRef                      IN, ///< Key reference
    KeyUsage  keyUsage                    OUT ///< Key usage
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the maximum number of times that a key may be used between system reboots.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetKeyMaxUsesPerBoot
(
    Key    keyRef        IN,  ///< Key reference
    uint32 value         IN   ///< Uses per boot
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the minimum amount of time that elapses between allowed operations using a key.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetKeyMinSecondsBetweenOps
(
    Key    keyRef        IN,  ///< Key reference
    uint32 value         IN   ///< Seconds interval between allowed operations
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set application data to the key.
 *
 * When this attribute is provided to the key, the same data must be also provided through
 * taf_ks_CryptoSessionSetAppData() for each cryptographic operation using the key.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetKeyAppData
(
    Key   keyRef                IN,  ///< Key reference
    uint8 data[MAX_PACKET_SIZE] IN   ///< Data buffer to hold the application data
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the date and time at which the key becomes active. Prior to this time any attempt to use the
 * key will get failed.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetKeyActiveDateTime
(
    Key    keyRef        IN,  ///< Key reference
    uint64 value         IN   ///< Milliseconds since January 1, 1970.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the date and time at which the key expires for signing and encryption. After this time any
 * attempt to use a key for signing or encryption will get failed.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetKeyOriginationExpireDateTime
(
    Key    keyRef        IN,  ///< Key reference
    uint64 value         IN   ///< Milliseconds since January 1, 1970.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the date and time at which the key expires for verification and decryption. After this time
 * any attempt to use a key for verification and decryption will get failed.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetKeyUsageExpireDateTime
(
    Key    keyRef        IN,  ///< Key reference
    uint64 value         IN   ///< Milliseconds since January 1, 1970.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Provison or import a RSA encryption key value to the new created key.
 *
 * The impData parameter if provided shall hold PKCS#8 DER format of RSA key data for import.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned or the key is not suitable for this
 *       provision or the key is not created by the client.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ProvisionRsaEncKeyValue
(
    Key              keyRef                   IN, ///< Key reference
    RsaKeySize       keySize                  IN, ///< Key size, set 0 if impData is provided
    RsaEncPadding    padding                  IN, ///< Padding type of RSA encryption key
    uint8            impData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE] IN  ///< Imported key data
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Provision or import a RSA signing key value to the new created key.
 *
 * The impData parameter if provided shall hold PKCS#8 DER format of RSA key data for import.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned or the key is not suitable for this
 *       provision or the key is not created by the client.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ProvisionRsaSigKeyValue
(
    Key              keyRef                   IN, ///< Key reference
    RsaKeySize       keySize                  IN, ///< Key Size, set 0 if impData is provided
    RsaSigPadding    padding                  IN, ///< Padding type of RSA signing key
    uint8            impData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE] IN  ///< Imported key data
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Provision or import an ECDSA key value to the new created key.
 *
 * The impData parameter if provided shall hold PKCS#8 DER format of ECDSA key data for import.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned or the key is not suitable for this
 *       provision or the key is not created by the client.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ProvisionEcdsaKeyValue
(
    Key              keyRef                   IN, ///< Key reference
    EccKeySize       keySize                  IN, ///< ECC curve, set 0 if impData is provided
    Digest           digest                   IN, ///< Digest
    uint8            impData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE] IN  ///< Imported key data
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Provision or import an AES key value to the new created key.
 *
 * The impData parameter if provided shall hold the AES raw key data for import.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned or the key is not suitable for this
 *       provision or the key is not created by the client.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ProvisionAesKeyValue
(
    Key              keyRef                   IN, ///< Key reference
    AesKeySize       keySize                  IN, ///< AES key size, set 0 if impData is provided
    AesBlockMode     mode                     IN, ///< AES block mode
    uint8            impData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE] IN  ///< Imported key data
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Provision or import a HMAC key value to the new created key.
 *
 * The impData parameter if provided shall hold the HMAC raw key data for import.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is already provisioned or the key is not suitable for this
 *       provision or the key is not created by the client.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ProvisionHmacKeyValue
(
    Key              keyRef                   IN, ///< Key reference
    uint32           keySize                  IN, ///< HMAC Key Size, set 0 if impData is provided
    Digest           digest                   IN, ///< digest
    uint8            impData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE] IN  ///< Imported key data
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Create a crypto operation session for a key.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is not provisioned yet.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CryptoSessionCreate
(
    Key           keyRef      IN,     ///< Key to use for this crypto session.
    CryptoSession sessionRef  OUT     ///< Session reference.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the nonce or IVs for AES GCM, CBC, CTR for a crypto session. For AES GCM the nonce size must
 * be 12 bytes, for AES CBC, CTR the IV must be 16 bytes.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the session or the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is not provisioned yet or the session is not created by the
 *       client.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CryptoSessionSetAesNonce
(
    CryptoSession   sessionRef     IN,  ///< Session reference
    uint8 data[MAX_AES_NONCE_SIZE] IN   ///< Data buffer to hold the nonce or IV
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the Application data for a crypto session.
 *
 * This API must be called before taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart() if the key has set the attribute of
 * application data by taf_ks_SetKeyAppData().
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the session or the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is not provisioned yet or the session is not created by the
 *       client.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CryptoSessionSetAppData
(
    CryptoSession   sessionRef     IN,  ///< Session reference
    uint8 data[MAX_PACKET_SIZE]    IN   ///< Data buffer to hold the application data
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Start the crypto session for the given crypto operation. The crypto session will be automatically
 * deleted if error occurs.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the session or the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is not provisioned yet or the session is not created by the
 *       client.
 *     - LE_DUPLICATE if the session is already started.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CryptoSessionStart
(
    CryptoSession sessionRef         IN,  ///< Session reference
    CryptoPurpose cryptoPurpose      IN   ///< Crypto purpose
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Provide AEAD to a AES GCM crypto session started with taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart().
 * This API can be called for multiple times before taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcess(). And the crypto
 * session will be automatically deleted if error occurs.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the session or the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is not provisioned yet or the session is not created by the
 *       client, or the session is not started.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CryptoSessionProcessAead
(
    CryptoSession   sessionRef     IN,  ///< Session reference
    uint8 data[MAX_PACKET_SIZE]    IN   ///< Data buffer to hold the AEAD data
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Provides data to, and possibly receives output from, an runing crypto session started with
 * taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart(). It can be called for multiple times before taf_ks_CryptoSessionEnd()
 * is called. The crypto session will be automatically deleted if error occurs.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER if bad parameters.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the session or the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is not provisioned yet or the session is not created by the
 *       client, or the session is not started.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CryptoSessionProcess
(
    CryptoSession sessionRef               IN, ///< Session reference
    uint8   inputData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE]     IN, ///< InputData can be one of below 4 cases:
                                               ///< 1: Plain text for encryption session.
                                               ///< 2: Cipher text for decryption session.
                                               ///< 3: Message to sign for signing session.
                                               ///< 4: Message to verify for verification session.
    uint8   outputData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE]    OUT ///< OutputData can be one of below 3 cases:
                                               ///< 1: Encrypted data for encryption session.
                                               ///< 2: Decrypted data for decryption session.
                                               ///< 3: Shall set NULL for signing and verification
                                               ///     sessions.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Finalize the crypto session started with taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart(). This API shall be called
 * once all input data get processed by taf_ks_CryptoSessionProcess(), and the crypto session
 * will be then automatically deleted.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the session or the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is not provisioned yet or the session is not created by the
 *       client, or the session is not started.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CryptoSessionEnd
(
    CryptoSession sessionRef               IN, ///< Session reference
    uint8   inputData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE]     IN, ///< Signature to verify for verification session
                                               ///< and shall set to NULL for other sessions.
    uint8   outputData[MAX_PACKET_SIZE]    OUT ///< OutputData can be one of below 4 cases:
                                               ///< 1: Encrypted data for encryption session.
                                               ///< 2: Decrypted data for decryption session.
                                               ///< 3: Signature for signing session.
                                               ///< 4: Shall set to NULL for verfication session.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Abort the crypto session started with taf_ks_CryptoSessionStart(), and the crypto session will be
 * then automatically deleted.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK if successful.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND if the session or the key doesn't exist.
 *     - LE_NOT_PERMITTED if the key is not provisioned yet or the session is not created by the
 *       client, or the session is not started.
 *     - LE_FAULT if error occurs.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CryptoSessionAbort
(
    CryptoSession sessionRef               IN  ///< Session reference
);
